msgid "Who may read the site: bot list, AI crawlers, allowed and blocked lists."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1472
msgid "Scrapers and bots"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1475
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:50
msgid "Block requests without a User-Agent"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1476
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:51
msgid "Block fake Googlebot, Bingbot, Applebot and Yandex"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1476
msgid "Checks the IP against the official lists and with reverse DNS."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1476
msgid "The IP is checked against the official Google and Bing lists and with reverse DNS. Real search engines always pass, without limits."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1477
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:136
msgid "Browsers only: 403 for pages without Accept-Language or without “Mozilla/” in the User-Agent"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1477
msgid "Stops most scripts; link previews in “Always allowed” still pass."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1477
msgid "Stops most scripts. Link previews (Facebook, Viber, WhatsApp etc.) in the “Always allowed” list pass."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1478
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:53
msgid "Block headless and fake browsers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1478
msgid "Catches HeadlessChrome and, on HTTPS, Chrome look-alikes without Sec-Fetch headers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1478
msgid "Blocks Chrome running without a window when it says so in its headers (“HeadlessChrome”), and, on HTTPS, scripts that copy the User-Agent of Chrome, Edge or Firefox without the Sec-Fetch headers every modern browser sends. It catches common tools and cheap scrapers, not every automated browser: one that is carefully disguised (e.g. Puppeteer with “stealth”, or Selenium with a visible Chrome) sends the same headers as a person. The page limits, the human check and the bot trap still apply to those. In-app browsers (Android WebView) are not checked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1479
#: includes/class-pncp-log.php:333
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:166
#: includes/class-pncp-status.php:451
msgid "Bot trap"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1479
msgid "A hidden link, disallowed in robots.txt; whoever opens it is blocked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1479
msgid "Invisible link on every page, disallowed in robots.txt. Whoever opens it is blocked temporarily, even if it pretends to be a browser. Visitors do not see it, and another site cannot trap them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1481
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:119
#: includes/class-pncp-wizard.php:1086
msgid "Ban scanners on their first probe"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1481
msgid "10-minute block on the first request for .env, .git, dumps and similar."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1481
msgid "Blocks an IP for 10 minutes the first time it asks for a file that only attack scanners look for and that does not exist on this site: .env, .git, backup copies of wp-config.php, database dumps and backup archives at the top of the site, SSH keys, phpMyAdmin, Adminer, PHP files in the uploads folder, and what scanners look for in other software (Spring Boot /actuator, Dockerfile and docker-compose files, credentials and secrets files, .aws, .vscode/sftp.json). A second probe within 24 hours gets the full temporary block. phpMyAdmin, Adminer and PHP files in uploads are caught only when the web server passes those requests to WordPress: Nginx usually answers a missing .php file itself, and “No PHP in uploads” refuses them first. Staff, verified search engines, the always-allowed IPs and User-Agents, and people who click a link or type the address in a browser are never blocked. On Nginx, add the updated rules from the “Server rules” tab so that requests for hidden files (.env, .git) reach WordPress."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1482
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:68
msgid "User-Agents to block (one per line, matches anywhere in the User-Agent, case-insensitive):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1482
msgid "Includes AI training crawlers and AI search bots; search can be allowed below."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1482
msgid "It contains two AI categories: training crawlers (GPTBot, ClaudeBot, CCBot, Google-Extended etc.) and AI search / assistants (OAI-SearchBot, ChatGPT-User, Claude-SearchBot, PerplexityBot etc.). You can allow the second one in the next section."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: number of AI crawlers
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1482
#, php-format
msgid "In addition, %s more AI crawlers and agents (DeepSeek, Grok, Qwen, Mistral, NotebookLM and others) are blocked by name: that list is built into ScrapeLock and updated with each version, so it is not shown here. A line that starts with “=” must be the whole User-Agent, e.g. “=node”."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: number of AI crawlers
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1483
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:54
msgid "Also block generic HTTP libraries (strict)"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: number of AI crawlers
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1483
msgid "Blocks curl, python-requests and similar, which apps and monitors also use."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: number of AI crawlers
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1483
msgid "Blocks the User-Agent that programming libraries send by default: curl, Wget, python-requests, Go, Java, okhttp, Dart, node-fetch, axios, Guzzle and others. Many cheap scrapers use them, but so do WooCommerce mobile apps (Flutter, Android), headless front ends, ERP and price sync, and uptime monitors. Turn it on only if nothing like that reads your site, or add those services to “Always allowed” first."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: list of User-Agents, e.g. "curl/, okhttp, Dart/"
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1491
#, php-format
msgid "Your bot list still blocks these HTTP libraries, even with this off: %s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1496
msgid "Lists saved before ScrapeLock 3.4 had them by default. If a mobile app, a headless front end or a sync service gets a 403, remove those lines from the list, or allow the service in “Always allowed”."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1499
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:60
msgid "Block SEO and marketing data crawlers (Ahrefs, Semrush, Majestic…)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1499
msgid "Backlink and competitor-research crawlers. Leave off if you use one."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: list of User-Agents
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1499
#, php-format
msgid "They are not search engines: backlink indexes and competitor research tools crawl hard and sell what they collect, to your competitors too. Blocked and asked in robots.txt: %s. Leave it off if you use one of these tools for your own site, or add its audit bot to “Always allowed”."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1501
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:61
msgid "Block technology profilers (BuiltWith, Wappalyzer, WhatCMS…)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1501
msgid "Services that list the CMS, theme and plugins a site runs."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: list of User-Agents
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1501
#, php-format
msgid "They are not search engines and send no visitors: they read the site to list its software (CMS, theme, plugins, server) and sell or publish that list, which also tells attackers where a vulnerable plugin runs. Blocked and asked in robots.txt: %s. Leave it off if you use one of these services for your own site, or add it to “Always allowed”."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: list of User-Agents
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1502
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:56
msgid "Refuse requests that open the site by its IP address instead of its name"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: list of User-Agents
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1502
msgid "Scanners sweep IP ranges; people and search engines use the domain name."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: list of User-Agents
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1502
msgid "Scanners that sweep whole address ranges ask for http://203.0.113.5/ instead of your domain; people and search engines follow links, which carry the name. Requests for a private address (a load balancer's health check, a reverse proxy) and a site that is set up with its IP as its address are never refused. Always on in Emergency Mode."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: number of programs
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1508
#, php-format
msgid "With the bot list on, %s site rippers and attack User-Agents are blocked too."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1513
msgid "Rippers and address harvesters such as HTTrack, WebCopier, Teleport Pro, Offline Explorer, SiteSucker and Octoparse, and any User-Agent that carries an attack instead of a name (HTML tags, Shellshock, Log4Shell, SQL injection): no browser or crawler sends one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1516
msgid "AI search and training"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1518
msgid "Appear in AI search answers with a link, without feeding model training."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: list of User-Agents
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1518
#, php-format
msgid "So the site appears in AI search answers with a link, without being given for model training. Allowed: %s. They are also removed from the robots.txt Disallow and from the server rules. The page limit still applies, because the User-Agent can be spoofed. While this is off, ScrapeLock blocks them, also when they are not in the bot list."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: list of User-Agents
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1519
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:174
msgid "Verify AI search bots with their official IP lists (OpenAI, Perplexity, Anthropic)"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: list of User-Agents
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1519
msgid "Real OpenAI, Perplexity and Anthropic search bots pass; impostors get a 403."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: list of User-Agents
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1519
msgid "With AI search allowed: the real OAI-SearchBot, ChatGPT-User, PerplexityBot, Perplexity-User, Claude-SearchBot and Claude-User are never limited or blocked, and requests that only use their name get a 403 (“Fake AI search bot”). The lists are downloaded once a day; until then nothing changes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1520
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:138
msgid "Declare AI crawlers in robots.txt (Disallow)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1520
msgid "Only the virtual robots.txt; a physical robots.txt file takes precedence."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1521
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:46
msgid "Block web archives (Wayback Machine)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1521
msgid "Blocks the Internet Archive crawlers; pages already archived stay there."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1521
msgid "The Internet Archive keeps a public copy of every page it visits, and that copy can be scraped without ever reaching your site. This blocks its crawlers (ia_archiver, archive.org_bot, heritrix) and asks them in robots.txt. Copies already in the archive stay there. Leave it off if you want your site to be archived."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1522
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:78
msgid "Content Signals in robots.txt: search yes, AI training no"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1522
msgid "Says search=yes, ai-train=no: a statement of terms, not a block."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1522
msgid "A line that says what the content may be used for (contentsignals.org): search=yes, ai-train=no, and ai-input according to “Allow AI search engines”. It does not block anything; it is a statement of your terms that well-behaved companies read."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1527
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:37
msgid "Always allowed User-Agents (link previews, price comparison platforms, monitoring):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1527
msgid "Overrides the bot list and “Browsers only”; the page limit still applies."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1527
msgid "They override the bot list and “Browsers only”. The page limit applies to them too, because the User-Agent is easy to spoof. To accept an entry only from specific IPs, add @ and the addresses, e.g. Skroutz@203.0.113.0/24."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1528
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:36
msgid "Always allowed IPs / CIDR (office, ERP, monitoring), one per line:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1528
msgid "Never checked, never limited, never blocked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1534
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:57
msgid "IPs / CIDR that are always blocked (403), one per line:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1534
msgid "For example a scraper's server from the log; “Always allowed IPs” win."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1535
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:58
msgid "Referrer domains that are always blocked (403), one per line, e.g. copy-site.example:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1535
msgid "Requests from links or embeds on these sites, subdomains included."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1536
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:65
msgid "Hide usernames from visitors"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1536
msgid "?author=N, the REST API and the users sitemap stop showing usernames."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1536
msgid "?author=1, 2, 3… returns “page not found” instead of the redirect to /author/username/, the REST API does not list users, the users sitemap is removed and oEmbed shows the site instead of the author. Logged-in users see everything as before. Author archives with a link stay."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1540
msgid "Pages per minute, stricter limits for some visitors, and temporary blocks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1541
msgid "Limits per IP"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1543
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:120
msgid "Pages per minute (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1543
msgid "429 above it. Behind a CDN, set “Real visitor IP” first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1543
msgid "Above the limit it returns 429. Be careful with networks that share an IP (companies, mobile carriers) and with CDNs: set the “Real visitor IP” correctly first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1544
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:131
msgid "Searches (?s=) per minute (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1544
msgid "Search is heavy for the server and a favourite of scrapers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1545
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:130
msgid "REST API (/wp-json/) and GraphQL requests per minute (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1545
msgid "Visitor read requests only; long per_page lists count as 2 or 3."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1545
msgid "Only read requests from visitors. Cart, checkout and forms (POST) do not count. A list of more than 20 items (per_page) counts as 2 requests, more than 50 as 3."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1551
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:121
msgid "“Page not found” (404) per minute (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1551
msgid "Catches address guessing; missing images, CSS and scripts do not count."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1551
msgid "Scrapers guess addresses (?p=1, 2, 3…, old product URLs) to find content. Missing images, CSS, scripts and the favicon do not count."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1552
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:132
msgid "Sitemaps per minute (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1552
msgid "Scrapers read sitemaps first; verified search engines are never limited."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1552
msgid "Scrapers read the sitemap first to find every page. Covers the sitemaps of WordPress, Rank Math, Yoast and similar plugins. Google, Bing and the other verified search engines are never limited."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1554
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:123
msgid "REST API, GraphQL, feeds and sitemaps per minute for IPs that never opened a page (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1554
msgid "For IPs that read only the API, feeds or sitemaps, never pages."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1554
msgid "Many scrapers skip the HTML and read only the API, the feeds or the sitemaps. A visitor opens a page first; such a scraper never does. An IP that has not opened a page of the site in the last 24 hours (nor passed the human check, nor signed in) gets this limit on those addresses, on top of the others. Feed readers and apps that read the API from their own servers count here too: add them to “Always allowed”. A headless front end that reads the REST API from its server needs its IP in “Always allowed IPs”. With a page cache plugin, cached pages do not reach WordPress and so are not seen: turn on the pre-cache check or the human check, or keep this limit at 20 or more. Suggested value: 10."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1555
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:101
msgid "IPv6: also limit the whole /56 network (four times the page limit)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1555
msgid "Also counts the whole /56, up to four times the page limit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1555
msgid "Pages are counted per /64, because one connection usually gets a whole /64. A server or a home connection often has a /56 or more, so a scraper can take a new /64 for every request. This also counts the /56 the /64 belongs to, up to four times the page limit (429 above it, without a block). Some mobile networks give neighbouring phones addresses of the same /56: on a site with many visitors from them, keep it off. Always on in Emergency Mode."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1556
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:128
msgid "Pages per minute from data centers (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1556
msgid "Cloud servers (AWS, Google Cloud…) get this instead; 5 in Emergency Mode."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1556
msgid "People rarely browse from a server; scrapers very often run on one. Visitors from the published addresses of AWS, Google Cloud, Oracle Cloud, DigitalOcean and Akamai / Linode get this stricter limit instead of the normal one. The lists are downloaded from the providers once a day. Some VPNs use these providers, so their users get this limit too: it is meant for reading, not for blocking. The always-allowed User-Agents (monitoring, price platforms) and verified search engines are not affected. 5 in Emergency Mode."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1558
#: includes/class-pncp-setting-labels.php:124
msgid "WooCommerce cart and checkout actions per minute (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1558
msgid "Cart, coupon and order actions; shoppers need a few, bots hundreds."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1558
