msgid "When “Import attacks from Bunny CDN's logs” is on, this site downloads the logs of its own Bunny CDN pull zone (logging.bunnycdn.com) every 15 minutes. They contain the IP address, the address asked for, the referrer, the browser identification (User-Agent) and the country of each request. Only requests that look like attacks are kept, with the IP address, for as long as the attack record is kept; the rest is discarded at once. When a vulnerable address is locked at Bunny CDN, the IP addresses administrators used in the last 30 days may be sent to the site owner's Bunny account, so that they are let through."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-bunny.php:4640
msgid "For the IP addresses whose requests looked like attacks or asked for an address that can be locked at Bunny CDN (such as wp-login.php or xmlrpc.php), the number of those requests and of the normal pages they opened through Bunny is also kept, for 8 days, so that ScrapeLock can show what a lock would refuse and warn before it refuses a real visitor."
msgstr ""

