msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:243
msgid "Visitors get an empty /wp-json/ route list; every route still works."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:243
msgid "Rare: an outside tool that discovers the API while signed out."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:244
msgid "No PHP file in the uploads folder ever runs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:244
msgid "Only a plugin that runs its own PHP from uploads (very rare)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:245
msgid "The server refuses PHP files in wp-includes opened directly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:245
msgid "Nothing on a normal site; ms-files.php stays open on multisite."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:246
msgid "The server refuses PHP files under wp-content opened by address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:246
msgid "Plugins with their own PHP address break: test payments and forms after."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:247
msgid "Folders without an index file answer 403 instead of a file list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:247
msgid "Nothing for visitors; the self-test reverts it if the host refuses."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:248
msgid "Closes pingback.ping, used for DDoS and for probing pages."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:248
msgid "You no longer receive pingbacks; trackbacks and comments still work."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:249
msgid "Adds nosniff, a strict Referrer-Policy and a Permissions-Policy header."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:249
msgid "Pages that use the camera, microphone or location stop asking for them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:250
msgid "Other sites cannot show your pages inside their iframe."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:250
msgid "Only if you frame your own pages on another site of yours."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:264
msgid "Refuses every request to xmlrpc.php. Bots use it to try hundreds of passwords in one request (system.multicall) and to make the site attack others with pingbacks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:266
msgid "Jetpack, the WordPress mobile app and old publishing tools (Windows Live Writer, some IFTTT recipes) use XML-RPC. With “Allow Jetpack” on, Jetpack's own servers still get through, without pingbacks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:274
msgid "wp-admin for visitors"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:275
msgid "Visitors who are not signed in get “page not found” for /wp-admin/ instead of a redirect to the login page, so bots do not learn that the site runs WordPress or where to log in. admin-ajax.php and admin-post.php keep working."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:277
msgid "A link to a wp-admin page (in an email or a bookmark) opens “page not found” until you sign in: open the login page first. /admin, /dashboard and /login no longer lead to the login page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:286
msgid "Limits failed logins per IP and moves the login page to an address of your own, so password-guessing bots find nothing at wp-login.php."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:288
msgid "Write down the new login address: the old one answers “page not found”. Plugins that link to wp-login.php are sent to the new address. “Open again” moves the login page back to wp-login.php and keeps the limit of failed logins on (turn it off on the Bots tab)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:297
msgid "readme.html, license.txt, wp-config-sample.php, wp-admin/install.php and setup-config.php answer “page not found”, and wp-admin/upgrade.php does too for visitors who are not signed in. Scanners open them to see that the site runs WordPress, which version, and whether it can still be installed again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:299
msgid "Nothing a visitor uses. The “Update database” screen after a WordPress update still works for signed-in administrators (Apache); on Nginx run “wp core update-db” instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:318
msgid "Theme and plugin file editor"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:319
msgid "Nobody can edit theme or plugin code from wp-admin (Appearance → Theme File Editor, Plugins → Plugin File Editor). Someone who steals an administrator password usually puts a backdoor in there first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:321
msgid "The two editor screens disappear. Edit files over SFTP or with your host's file manager instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:332
msgid "Application passwords for non-administrators"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:333
msgid "Only administrators can create and use application passwords (REST API and XML-RPC logins without the normal login page). A stolen editor or customer account cannot be turned into a permanent API key."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:335
msgid "An app or service that signs in with the application password of an editor, author or shop manager (a mobile app, Zapier, a publishing tool) stops working. Administrators are not affected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:343
msgid "Usernames: ?author=N and REST /wp/v2/users"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:344
msgid "Bots collect the usernames of the site with ?author=1, 2, 3… and /wp-json/wp/v2/users, then try passwords for them. Visitors get “page not found” and an empty list (the setting “Hide usernames from visitors”)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:346
msgid "Nothing for visitors; signed-in users see everything as before. The users sitemap is removed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:354
msgid "Author archives (/author/name/)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:355
msgid "The author pages show each username in their address. For visitors they answer “page not found”, and links to them point to the home page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:357
msgid "Author pages leave search results, and a theme that shows “More posts by this author” links to the home page. Sites with several authors who have their own pages should leave this off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:365
msgid "REST API map (/wp-json/)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:366
msgid "/wp-json/ lists every route of every plugin: a map of what to attack. Visitors get an empty list and no links to it; each route still works (the setting “Hide the REST API map”)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:368
msgid "Rare: an outside tool that discovers the API from /wp-json/ while not signed in. The block editor and signed-in users are not affected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:376
msgid "PHP in the uploads folder"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:377
msgid "A backdoor uploaded through a vulnerable plugin usually lands in the uploads folder. No PHP file there ever runs (the setting “No PHP in the uploads folder”; on Apache ScrapeLock writes it into the uploads folder's .htaccess, on Nginx it needs the rule below)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:379
msgid "Only a plugin that runs its own PHP from the uploads folder (very rare)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:387
msgid "PHP files in wp-includes, opened directly"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:388
msgid "The PHP files in wp-includes are never meant to be opened in a browser; scanners open them to find errors that show the server's folders, or old bugs. The server refuses them (the classic editor's wp-tinymce.php stays open)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:390
msgid "Nothing in a normal site. On a multisite network that still serves files through ms-files.php, that file stays open."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:398
msgid "PHP files in wp-content, opened directly"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:399
msgid "Scanners call the PHP files of plugins and themes directly, looking for the ones with known holes (file uploaders, old image scripts). The server refuses every PHP file under wp-content that is opened by its address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:401
msgid "Plugins and themes that have their own PHP address (some captchas, image resizers, download counters, payment callbacks of older gateways) stop working. Test the site, the shop's payment and the forms right after, or add the files to the filter pncp_harden_php_allow."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:409
msgid "Directory listing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:410
msgid "A folder without an index file (wp-includes, uploads, a plugin's folder) can show the list of its files. The server answers 403 instead, so nobody browses the files of the site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:412
msgid "Nothing a visitor uses. Some hosts do not allow “Options” in .htaccess; the self-test then puts the file back on its own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:420
msgid "XML-RPC pingbacks"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:421
msgid "pingback.ping stays open even when XML-RPC is “off”, and is used to make the site send requests to other sites (DDoS) or to check that a page exists (the setting “Turn off XML-RPC pingbacks”). Other XML-RPC methods keep working."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:423
msgid "Other blogs can no longer tell you they linked to you with a pingback. Trackbacks and comments are not affected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:431
msgid "Security headers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:432
msgid "X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff (an uploaded file is never run as a script), Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin (other sites do not see your full addresses and their query strings) and Permissions-Policy (no camera, microphone or location for scripts on your pages)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:434
msgid "A page that uses the visitor's camera, microphone or location (a store finder with “Use my location”, a video chat) stops asking for it. Leave it off then, or change the header with the filter pncp_harden_headers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:442
msgid "Framing by other sites (X-Frame-Options)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:443
msgid "Other sites cannot show your pages inside their own iframe (click-jacking, copied pages under another address). The setting “Pages do not open inside another site's iframe”."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-hardening.php:445
msgid "Only if you show your own pages inside another site of yours. WordPress embeds (oEmbed) keep working."
msgstr ""

