msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-lockdown.php:4908
msgid "No other folder of wp-content can be written either. With the weaker lock, this page then shows a line to add to wp-config.php by hand, define( 'SCRAPELOCK_LOCKED', '...' ); (signed with this site's keys): with it, if someone deletes or changes the Lockdown data in the database, the site stays locked, protected settings are put back while their saved copy is there and the alert goes to the address signed when you locked. Until the line is there, everything about the lock is kept in the database only: someone who can change the database directly can delete all of it, and the site then looks as if it had never been locked. This cannot be noticed or reported."
