#: includes/class-pncp-log.php:2050
msgid "To protect content from automated copying, when a request is blocked we record the IP address, the browser's User-Agent, the page and the time. This data is deleted automatically after a few days and is not used for any other purpose."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-log.php:2051
msgid "If blocking at the CDN is turned on, the IP addresses that are blocked temporarily are also sent to our CDN provider (Cloudflare or Bunny CDN), with a short note that gives the reason and the end of the block, so the CDN can refuse them before they reach our server. Each one is removed from the CDN when the block ends. Nothing else about visitors is sent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-log.php:2052
msgid "So that administrators are never blocked by mistake, the IP addresses from which administrators used the site's dashboard in the last 30 days are kept; older ones are deleted automatically."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-log.php:2054
msgid "If IP reputation is turned on, for each IP address (stored only as a one-way hash) we keep, for up to 7 days, when it last read pages, passed the automatic human check, was used to sign in, or was refused or blocked, to treat it more or less strictly. We count visits that come from AI assistants (such as ChatGPT or Perplexity) per day and page only, without any data about the visitor."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-log.php:2055
msgid "If the CrowdSec blocklist is turned on, we download a list of IP addresses known for attacks and check visitors against it on our server; no data about visitors is sent to CrowdSec or the list's provider. If writing blocks to the system log is turned on, the IP addresses that are blocked temporarily are also written to our server's system log, so the server's firewall can block them for the same time."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-log.php:2057
msgid "To see where the site is attacked, for failed sign-ins, visits to the sign-in page or the dashboard without signing in, XML-RPC calls and requests that look for weak points, we record the IP address, the address asked for, the time (per hour) and, for a failed sign-in, the username that was tried. This is deleted automatically after 7, 30 or 90 days and is not used for any other purpose."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-log.php:2058
msgid "If the weekly attack report is turned on, a summary of the attack record (counts, the addresses attacked, the IP addresses that attacked most and the usernames tried) is emailed once a week to the site's administration email address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-log.php:2060
msgid "When a vulnerable point is locked (Vulnerable points), refused requests to it (XML-RPC, wp-admin while signed out, author archives) are written to the block log with the visitor's IP address and User-Agent, like other blocks. The list of changes keeps the username of the administrator who made each change."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-log.php:2062
msgid "When a signed-in member goes over a per-account limit, the block log also keeps the member's username with that entry, deleted with the rest of the log."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-log.php:2067
msgid "When you are signed in, ScrapeLock sets a cookie named pncp_si with the value 1 in your browser, so that this site's pages can tell that you are signed in even when they come from a cache. It contains no personal data, is removed when you sign out and lasts no longer than your sign-in."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-log.php:2068
msgid "ScrapeLock Stealth changes the addresses of the theme, plugin and media files in the pages sent to visitors. It stores no data about visitors. Its self-test and scan only request this site's own public pages, from the site itself."
msgstr ""

