#: includes/class-pncp-stealth.php:2723
msgid "Tools like BuiltWith and Wappalyzer, and the scanners that look for known holes, first find out what a site is built with: from the addresses of the theme and plugin files (/wp-content/, /wp-includes/), the REST API (/wp-json/), the sitemap (/wp-sitemap.xml), markup only WordPress prints and files only WordPress has. With Stealth, visitors get neutral addresses instead (for example /assets/3fa9c1/style.css), served by rules of your web server. Nothing stored changes: turning it off puts everything back at once."
